From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glebn2 <40612835+glebn2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: WPA3 (SAE) on the stock 4.19 kernel of BALMUDA Phone

cfg80211 of the stock Kyocera 4.19 kernel rejects NL80211_WPA_VERSION_3
in CONNECT with -EINVAL before the driver sees it, which Android reports
as a wrong password: no SAE network (WPA3-only or WPA2/WPA3) could be
joined. Send NL80211_WPA_VERSION_2 for RSN like the stock Android 11
supplicant did; the qcacld driver detects SAE from the AKM and requests
external auth, and wpa_supplicant runs SAE (including H2E).
---
 src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
index af544ab..c6d93fa 100644
--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -3845,7 +3845,9 @@ static int wpa_ver_supported(struct wpa_driver_nl80211_data *drv,
 			* NL80211_ATTR_SAE_PASSWORD is related and was added
 			* at the same time as NL80211_WPA_VERSION_3.
 			*/
-			if (nl80211_attr_supported(drv, NL80211_ATTR_SAE_PASSWORD) &&
+			/* BALMUDA Phone: cfg80211 of the stock 4.19 kernel rejects NL80211_WPA_VERSION_3;
+			 * the driver detects SAE from the AKM and asks for external auth */
+			if (0 && nl80211_attr_supported(drv, NL80211_ATTR_SAE_PASSWORD) &&
 				wpa_key_mgmt_sae(key_mgmt_suites))
 				ver |= NL80211_WPA_VERSION_3;
 			else
